/**
 * VM_MOVE / VM_MOVE_CLEANUP — move one server's VM to another physical node.
 *
 * The engine (design in docs/VM-MOVE.md, operational plan in
 * docs/PRIMARY-OFFLOAD-PLAN.md). Facts and decisions come from lib/vm-move/*;
 * this file only sequences side effects and records what happened on the
 * server's VmMove row so a retried job resumes instead of restarting.
 *
 * Phase order and WHY it is this order:
 *   SNAPSHOT_LIVE → SEND_FULL      source keeps running; the big transfer costs
 *                                  the customer nothing.
 *   STOP_SOURCE                    dark window opens. Server.status is set to
 *                                  STOPPED here on purpose: vmRecoverySweep
 *                                  restarts any RUNNING server whose VM is off,
 *                                  which would resurrect the source mid-move.
 *   SEND_INCREMENTAL               only what changed since the full pass.
 *   CREATE_TARGET                  config via the Proxmox API + move-safe
 *                                  cloud-init snippet (lib/vm-move/plan.ts
 *                                  explains why the original snippet must NOT
 *                                  be reused).
 *   MOVE_IP (dedicated only)       the one step with an external side effect;
 *                                  deliberately last before start so everything
 *                                  before it rolls back locally.
 *   START_TARGET                   start + guest agent + SSH verify.
 *   COMMIT                         DB cutover, NAT reconcile on both nodes, DNS
 *                                  resync, source onboot=0, notices, audit.
 *
 * Failure policy: before STOP_SOURCE a failure just re-queues the job (the
 * source is still serving; the resume continues from the last checkpoint).
 * Between STOP_SOURCE and COMMIT a failure rolls back IMMEDIATELY (target
 * removed, IP routed back, source started) to keep the dark window short.
 * From COMMIT on the move is forward-only (the DB already points at the
 * target) and a failure re-queues for a retry of the idempotent remainder.
 *
 * The source VM is never destroyed here. VM_MOVE_CLEANUP, requested
 * explicitly after `keepSourceUntil`, does that — and only after re-verifying
 * the DB and the hypervisor both agree the target is the live one.
