    // resize/start, no OVH allocation, no cloud-init snippet write. `vmid` IS
    // still allocated for real (via `allocateSandboxVmid`, see its doc comment
    // in lib/ipam.ts) — this used to be the racy inline `990000 +
    // (await db.server.count())`, which handed two servers the identical vmid
    // whenever no other Server row was created between their two provisioning
    // runs (the common case: rows are inserted at checkout, well before the
    // PROVISION job runs), and the second `prisma.server.update()` below died
    // on the `vmid` unique constraint. Only for a fresh allocation — a retry
    // keeps whatever vmid a previous attempt already claimed, same rule the
    // real Proxmox path follows just below in the non-sandbox branch.
