  // a retry: `destroyVm` just above genuinely deletes the VM, so the guest
  // that "already saw" the old password no longer exists — the next one is a
  // brand-new instance that has never seen ANY password yet. Without this,
  // reinstall silently kept the customer's old root password forever (found
  // in the 2026-09-24 audit) — the one operation a customer expects to rotate
  // credentials (e.g. after a suspected compromise) quietly didn't. Nulling
  // both columns here makes `serverRootPassword(server)` return null once
  // provision() reloads the row, so its existing `?? generatePassword()`
  // fallback mints a real fresh one — same code path a first-ever provision
  // takes, no new logic needed there.
  await db.server.update({
    where: { id: server.id },
